the average person eats about 40  kilograms of meat per year in developed  countries it's double that or about the  same weight as an adult dolphin what  experts now advise cutting down the  amount of meat we eat to help reduce  climate change so here's a thought  experiment what if the whole world  turned vegan around 15 percent of all  greenhouse gases emitted by humans are  from livestock production if you'll  became vegan these emissions would be  slashed eating meat takes up space a lot  of us and 80% of all farmland is  dedicated to meat and dairy production  that's about the size of Europe at the  US China and Australia combined nice and  dairy typically provide 18% of our  calories but account for 60% of  greenhouse gas emissions from  agriculture  a report by the UN's Climate body the  IPCC recommends we all reduce the amount  of meat we eat and also how much we  waste the report found 8 to 10 percent  of all global emissions are down to food  loss and food waste but not all meat is  the same large-scale farming of beef has  a particularly high impact and has been  a big factor in the loss of the Amazon  rainforest when cows digest their food  they produce methane a powerful  greenhouse gas that's about 28 times  more powerful than carbon dioxide  over 100 years and when calves burp this  methane is emitted one cow releases  between 70 and 100 kilograms of methane  every year when they're around 1.5  billion cattle in the world today what  is not as simple a lot depends on how  the meat is produced most meat is  mass-produced by large-scale industry  and this can come with a heavy  environmental impact but small-scale  farming of animals can have a lower  environmental footprint and sometimes  for it  in the case of traditional grazing it  can be beneficial in terms of  biodiversity vegan alternatives can also  come with their own problems for example  large scale production of soya can lead  to deforestation when almond production  requires huge amounts of water but if  everyone switched to a plant-based diet  it could bring several positive health  benefits one study estimated that if  everyone ate a vegan diet with lots of  fresh fruit and vege around 8 million  deaths could be avoided around the world  by 2050 there are no simple answers but  if everyone were to change how they look  at food cultivated and eat it in a  sustainable way we could potentially  change the world thanks for watching  don't forget to subscribe and click the  bail to receive notifications for new  videos see you again soon
 

